<title>HONG KONG: Bouygues wins US$92 mln Thai contract.</title>
<headline>Bouygues wins US$92 mln Thai contract.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bouygues Thai, a subsidiary of French construction company Bouygues, said on Monday it has won a US$92 million contract from Bangkok Land Plc for the construction of a new leisure and sports complex.</p>
<p>The complex, with a total floor area of 80,000 square metres including a 10,000-seat arena and four exhibition halls, will host part of the Asian Games to take place in Bangkok in December 1998, a statement issued on behalf on Bouygues Thai said.</p>
<p>Works started at the end of January with delivery scheduled for July 1998, it said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
